---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/common/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const site=import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL?.replace(/\/$/,'');
const pageUrl=site?`${site}/editorial-policy/`:undefined;
const schema={
  '@type':'AboutPage',
  '@id':pageUrl?`${pageUrl}#policy`:undefined,
  name:'HisaabLab Editorial and Calculation Policy',
  url:pageUrl,
  about:{'@id':site?`${site}/#organization`:undefined},
  mainEntity:{'@type':'Organization','@id':site?`${site}/editorial-policy/#editorial`:undefined,name:'HisaabLab Editorial',url:pageUrl}
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial & Calculation Policy" description="How HisaabLab develops, tests, sources, reviews and corrects its financial calculators and educational guides." schema={schema}>
  <section class="simple-page"><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Editorial policy'}]} /><div class="simple-page-grid"><nav><a href="#purpose">Purpose</a><a href="#calculations">Calculations</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a><a href="#bylines">Bylines</a><a href="#corrections">Corrections</a><a href="#commercial">Commercial policy</a></nav><article class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Trust & transparency</span><h1 id="purpose">Editorial and calculation policy</h1><p class="lead">HisaabLab publishes free financial calculators and explanatory guides for Indian households. This page explains how the tools are built, what the editorial byline means and how corrections are handled.</p><p><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> 5 November 2026.</p><h2 id="calculations">How calculations are developed</h2><p>Each calculator uses a documented mathematical model implemented as TypeScript functions. The calculation engine carries full numerical precision internally and rounds values for display. Automated tests cover formulas, schedules, edge cases and the calculator registry before a production build can pass.</p><p>Calculator pages show their formula, timing convention, assumptions, limitations and an illustrative worked example. Inputs such as interest rates, appreciation and investment returns are editable scenarios—not forecasts or recommendations.</p><h2 id="sources">Sources and time-sensitive information</h2><p>Regulatory statements are kept narrow and linked to primary sources where practical, including the Reserve Bank of India. Source review dates are displayed on calculator pages. A review date means the linked material was checked on that date; it does not guarantee that a rule, lender policy or fee has remained unchanged afterward.</p><p>HisaabLab does not publish a single “current market rate” as though it applied to every borrower. Visitors should compare the calculator result with the lender’s current Key Facts Statement, sanction letter, repayment schedule and applicable official guidance.</p><h2 id="bylines">What “HisaabLab Editorial” means</h2><p>HisaabLab Editorial is the publishing byline for original site guides. It identifies the publisher and does not claim that the content is personalised advice or that the publisher is a bank, lender, broker, chartered accountant, lawyer or registered investment adviser.</p><p>Articles are designed to explain the site’s models, trade-offs and decision checks. They do not rank or recommend financial products, lenders or properties.</p><h2 id="corrections">Corrections and feedback</h2><p>Material calculation or factual errors should be corrected transparently. Article pages display their publication and update dates. If you find an issue, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and include the page, inputs used, result observed and result expected. Do not send account numbers, identity documents or other sensitive financial information.</p><h2 id="commercial">Commercial and advertising policy</h2><p>Calculators do not require an account, lead form or ad click. Advertising code remains inactive unless a publisher account, privacy disclosures and any applicable consent controls are configured. Advertising does not change calculator results or editorial conclusions.</p><h2>Use of HisaabLab</h2><p>All results are educational estimates. Financial contracts can use different day-count, fee, reset, tax and rounding conventions. Verify decisions with the relevant institution and an appropriately qualified professional when needed.</p></article></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
